//? Title: Linear congruential pseudorandom generation
//? Subtitle: Original8,43,218 recurrence, actual wrap evidence and bounded low-bit periods
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A mixed LCG is an unsigned affine recurrence. Its full-period theorem describes
how long the state cycle is, while low-bit cycles, predictability and lattice
structure are different questions. We retain the original
seed1/multiplier5/increment3 example, expose actual producing multiply/add
records, compare raw consumption with native affine jump composition and inspect
complete small-modulus orbits without pretending to traverse2^64 states.
)

\toc

> Unsigned affine dynamics

The recurrence is

$$x_{n+1}=a\,x_n+c\pmod{2^{64}}.$$
\alttext(Each actual raw step multiplies the current unsigned64 word, adds the increment and keeps the low64 bits.)

Defined unsigned overflow is exactly the intended modular reduction. The
full-period mixed-generator conditions for modulus2^64 are c odd and a
congruent1 modulo4. These are stricter than merely saying “custom odd
parameters”: the native engine constructor rejects multiplier3 and even
increments. Every seed is allowed. The theorem gives period2^64 for admitted
parameters; a short empirical trace is not evidence that every state was
visited, nor does a long period imply independent samples, security or good
low-bit behavior.

> Original three actual states

Retain seed1, multiplier5 and increment3. Three real native steps
return8,43,218. The shared next_step kernel records each original word, low64
product and committed output; ordinary next_u64 uses exactly that same producer.
The diagram reads those actual steps rather than evaluating a report-side
recurrence.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcg_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::random::LinearCongruential64 g(1, 5, 3);
    auto t = dm::random::lcg64_trace(g, 3);
    std::print("| actual original word | actual multiplier | actual low64 product | actual increment | " "actual committed word | actual product wrapped | actual add wrapped |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        auto &e = t.steps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.before,
                   e.multiplier, e.product, e.increment, e.after,
                   e.multiplication_wrapped, e.addition_wrapped);
        d.node(std::to_string(i), {6. * i, 0},
               std::format("Actual {}*{}+{}\nnew word{}", e.multiplier,
                           e.before, e.increment, e.after));
        if (i)
            d.edge(std::to_string(i - 1), std::to_string(i));
    }
    d.save_svg("build/lcg_original.svg");
}
```
