> Actual wrap and the short least-significant-bit cycle

The production engine validates full-period parameters, while the pure step
helper deliberately accepts arbitrary coefficients for arithmetic controls. At
state=a=c=UINT64_MAX, the actual low64 product is1 and adding UINT64_MAX wraps
to0; both wrap flags describe exact unsigned range overflow, not hardware
instruction flags.

For an admitted mixed engine, a and c are odd, so the least significant bit
obeys bit_next=bit_old+1 modulo2. It alternates deterministically with period2,
despite the full state’s period2^64. The next figure uses actual raw engine
words, projecting their low bits only for display. Full words remain printed; no
low-bit pattern is presented as independent randomness.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcg_low_bit.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto m = std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max();
    auto wrap = dm::random::lcg64_step(m, m, m);
    std::print("Actual full-range product {}; actual final word {}; multiplication wrapped {}; addition " "wrapped {}.\n\n| actual raw index | actual original word | actual new word | actual low bit " "| actual low4 residue |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               wrap.product, wrap.after, wrap.multiplication_wrapped,
               wrap.addition_wrapped);
    dm::random::LinearCongruential64 g(1, 5, 3);
    auto t = dm::random::lcg64_trace(g, 16);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        auto &e = t.steps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, e.before, e.after,
                   e.after & 1, e.after & 15);
        x.push_back(i + 1);
        y.push_back(e.after & 1);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual projected LSB", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, y, "",
                                                                  {37, 99, 235},
                                                                  5).y_limits(
        -.2, 1.5).title("Actual raw words have an alternating least significant bit").x_label("actual completed raw steps").y_label("low bit of actual new word").save_svg("build/lcg_low_bit.svg");
}
```
