> Jumping by affine composition

Represent an affine map by(a,c). Composition gives

$$(a,c)\circ(b,d)=(ab,ad+c)\pmod{2^{64}},\qquad(a,c)^2=(a^2,(a+1)c).$$
\alttext(Affine maps compose by multiplying multipliers and applying the outer multiplier to the inner increment before adding the outer increment.)

Binary exponentiation computes an exact jump using at most64 real composition
iterations for an unsigned64 count, without dividing by a−1 or replaying that
many raw steps. Its recorded stages are actual composition work, not a
fabricated raw history. Compare jumps at selected counts with words read from
one genuinely consumed1024-step trace. Zero count is the original seed. A jump
function is pure and does not mutate any engine or its inherited cached normal
draw.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcg_jump.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::random::LinearCongruential64 g(1, 5, 3);
    auto raw = dm::random::lcg64_trace(g, 1024);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual forward count | actual affine-jump result | actual raw-trace word | exact equality " "| actual composition iterations |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (std::uint64_t count : {0, 1, 2, 3, 8, 16, 64, 256, 1024}) {
        auto j = dm::random::lcg64_jump(1, 5, 3, count);
        const auto actual =
            count ? raw.steps[count - 1].after : raw.initial_state;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", count, j.after, actual,
                   j.after == actual, j.stages.size());
        x.push_back(count);
        y.push_back(j.stages.size());
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "affine iterations", {37, 99, 235}, 6).y_limits(0, 15).title(
        "Actual affine jump work, checked against one real raw trace").x_label(
        "requested forward raw-step count").y_label("actual composition-loop iterations").save_svg("build/lcg_jump.svg");
}
```
