> Complete small-modulus orbits and explicit failure controls

The low b bits form an autonomous recurrence modulo2^b: reducing a full unsigned
step and then masking is exactly the same modular dynamics. The native bounded
orbit helper computes that reduced recurrence directly without consuming a full
engine. It stops only on a real repeated residue or an explicit step budget, and
reports an incomplete prefix honestly.

For b1 through8, admitted a5,c3 has complete period2^b. At b4, pure diagnostic
controls a3,c1 and a5,c0 have shorter periods, while a5,c0 at seed0 is fixed.
The production constructor rejects those invalid full-period parameter controls;
their reduced orbit is still scientifically inspectable through the explicit
pure helper. A width20 orbit with only32 permitted steps is incomplete; no2^64
empirical period claim is inferred.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcg_orbits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual reduced width | actual complete | actual observed period | full-period theorem " "reference for this reduced modulus |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (unsigned b = 1; b <= 8; ++b) {
        auto o =
            dm::random::lcg64_low_bits_orbit(1, 5, 3, b, std::size_t{1} << b);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", b, o.complete, o.period,
                   std::size_t{1} << b);
        x.push_back(b);
        y.push_back(o.period);
    }
    std::print("\n| explicit seed | explicit a | explicit c | actual reduced4 period |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto parameters : std::vector<std::vector<std::uint64_t>>{{0, 3, 1},
                                                                   {1, 5, 0},
                                                                   {0, 5, 0}}) {
        auto o =
            dm::random::lcg64_low_bits_orbit(parameters[0], parameters[1],
                                             parameters[2], 4, 16);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", parameters[0], parameters[1],
                   parameters[2], o.period);
    }
    auto short_run = dm::random::lcg64_low_bits_orbit(1, 5, 3, 20, 32);
    std::print("\nActual width20 prefix: performed steps {}; complete {}; period placeholder {}.\n",
               short_run.states.size() - 1, short_run.complete, short_run.period);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "reduced periods", {37, 99, 235}, 6).y_limits(0, 350).title(
        "Actual small-modulus cycles, not a2^64 traversal").x_label(
        "projected low-bit width").y_label("observed complete reduced period").save_svg("build/lcg_orbits.svg");
}
```
